[
    {
        "id": "timespanexample",
        "type": "tab",
        "label": "price-timer time span",
        "disabled": false,
        "info": "Click sample prices. The whole-day node plans 2 hours for myhome/washing-machine. The 08:00-16:00 and 16:00-08:00 nodes both control myhome/boiler and only send output 2 during their own span."
    },
    {
        "id": "timespancomment",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "timespanexample",
        "name": "2 cheapest hours whole day",
        "info": "The sample series is cheapest at 03:00 (80) and 04:00 (90).\n\nClick \"sample prices\".\n\nWhole day runs 03:00-05:00 on topic myhome/washing-machine, from msg.topic.\n\nOutput 1 is the schedule. Output 2 is on or off for the current time.",
        "x": 460,
        "y": 80,
        "wires": []
    },
    {
        "id": "62f99c795b8f8f14",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "timespanexample",
        "name": "2 cheapest hours during night and 2 cheapest hours during daytime.",
        "info": "Today's series is cheapest at 03:00 (80) and 04:00 (90). msg.tomorrowPrices is cheapest at 01:00 (50) and 02:00 (60).\n\nClick \"sample prices\".\n\nWhen you trigger after 05:00, the 16:00-08:00 node prices morning hours from tomorrow, so it runs 01:00-03:00. Before those hours have ended today, it still uses today's morning prices (03:00-05:00).\nThe 08:00-16:00 node ignores tomorrow prices and runs 11:00-12:00 and 14:00-15:00.\n\nBoth nodes use topic myhome/boiler, which overrides myhome/washing-machine from the inject node. Both have Only during span enabled, and both control outputs join one debug node. Outside its span, a node sends nothing on output 2, so they do not turn each other off.\n\nStop when span ends is off because 16:00 and 08:00 meet. Enable it when there is a gap between spans, so the load gets one off command as a span finishes.\n\nOutput 1 is the schedule. Output 2 is on or off for the current time.\nTime span is exclusive at the end, so 08:00-16:00 covers 08:00 up to 16:00.",
        "x": 580,
        "y": 260,
        "wires": []
    },
